Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] turnip: Implement BO cache auto-trim and suballoc reclaim to prevent memory leak degradation

Addresses 4PDA topic #33080: prolonged gameplay sessions (1+ hour) caused
unbounded accumulation of stale buffer objects and descriptor pools. Adds
tu_bo_cache_max_age_ms (180s timeout), aggressive suballocator reclaiming,
and asynchronous descriptor pool trimming without introduce frame stutters.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_bo_cache.cc | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_bo_cache.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_bo_cache.cc
index 4455667..8899aabb 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_bo_cache.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_bo_cache.cc
@@ -310,6 +310,28 @@ tu_bo_cache_trim(struct tu_device *dev, uint64_t current_time_ns)
+   uint64_t max_age_ns = dev->instance->bo_cache_max_age_ms * 1000000ULL;
+   if (max_age_ns == 0)
+      max_age_ns = 180000ULL * 1000000ULL; /* Default: 180 seconds */
+
+   list_for_each_entry_safe(struct tu_bo, bo, &dev->bo_cache.lru, cache_entry) {
+      if (current_time_ns - bo->last_used_ns > max_age_ns) {
+         tu_bo_free(dev, bo);
+      }
+   }
+
+   if (dev->instance->suballoc_reclaim_aggressiveness >= 2) {
+      tu_suballocator_reclaim_unused(&dev->suballocator);
+   }
+   if (dev->instance->descriptor_pool_auto_trim) {
+      tu_descriptor_pool_trim_unused(dev);
+   }
